function validateWorkshop(input) {
  const fields = [];

  if (!input.title || typeof input.title !== "string") {
    fields.push("title");
  }

  if (typeof input.seats !== "number" || input.seats <= 0) {
    fields.push("seats");
  }

  return fields;
}

sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
A route can turn validation results into one stable client-error response.

```js
const fields = validateEvent(req.body);

if (fields.length > 0) {
  return res.status(400).json({
    error: "Validation failed",
    fields,
  });
}
```

**Step by step:** validate first, inspect the returned problems, and stop when any exist. A consistent `{ error, fields }` shape makes client behavior predictable. This is different from a missing resource and from an unexpected server failure.

